Mito Data Studio — No License Granted

PROJECT STATUS — LICENSE REVIEW IN PROGRESS

Mito Data Studio is under active development and license review. The current
project policy is to continue authorized internal development and hosted
research use while pausing external distribution of the integrated software,
including source releases, installation packages, and container images.
The project is not currently offered under an open-source license.

This status statement is not a general grant of permission for internal,
academic, research, or other use. Any separate authorization must come from
the relevant rights holders and remains subject to applicable third-party
licenses. Access to a hosted instance does not itself grant a license to
copy, modify, or redistribute the software.

FIRST-PARTY CODE AND DOCUMENTATION

Except where a separate license or authorization applies, no permission is
granted by this notice to copy, modify, distribute, sublicense, or create
derivative works from first-party Mito Data Studio code or documentation.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS AND UNRESOLVED REVIEW

Third-party components retain their own licenses. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and
docs/attribution.md, together with the license files accompanying vendored
components and installed dependencies.

The measurement implementation currently uses kimimaro 5.8.5, licensed under
GPL-3.0-or-later, and includes other GPL/LGPL dependencies. The licensing
requirements for distribution of the integrated software remain under review.
The upstream licensing and redistribution terms of the Cellable-derived
modules also require verification before an external release is approved.

